& [PlacementPlanContract] is strict and bounded
  + [profile] is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-regular-file-topology-projection/0.1
  + [projection_identity] is a nonzero caller-owned u64
  + [entry_reference_identity] is a nonzero caller-owned u64
  + [relative_path] is a required String later validated as an M2A descendant path
  + [mode_class] is a required TopologyModeClass
  + [observation_ordinal] is a nonzero caller-owned u64
  + [encoded_plan_cap] is exactly 262144 bytes before JSON decode
  = must: serde JSON denies unknown fields, omissions, wrong types, malformed scalars, and unknown enum variants
  - never: include metadata, digest, binding, seed, root, handle, clock, or claimed provenance in the plan

& [PlanValidationContract] is deterministic
  + validate exact profile first after decode
  + validate projection_identity nonzero
  + validate entry_reference_identity nonzero
  + accept mode_class exactly regular_non_executable or regular_executable
  + reject directory mode
  + validate observation_ordinal nonzero
  + relative-path grammar is not duplicated here and is enforced by current M2A validation on the completed candidate

& [BindingInputContract] preserves prerequisite authority
  + [input] is one WindowsSuppliedContentStableBinding passed by value
  + [construction] remains available only through the signed supplied-content binding path
  + [entry_reference] reads the binding content-observation entry-reference identity
  + [stable_pair] reads the complete nested stable pair
  + [seed] derives only through stable_pair.pre_read.topology_projection_seed
  - never: accept serialized binding JSON, asserted digest text, standalone digest observation, standalone stable pair, or standalone projection seed
  - never: add Deserialize, Default, public fields, or a public constructor to the prerequisite binding

& [EntryReferenceJoinContract] is exact
  + require plan.entry_reference_identity equals binding.content_observation.entry_reference_identity
  + prerequisite authority already requires that binding identity equals stable-pair common entry-reference identity
  + mismatch returns entry_reference fault before successful projection release
  - never: interpret equality as physical object, path, handle, file, process, global, durable, or authenticated identity

& [ProjectionMappingContract] is closed
  + call topology_projection_seed on binding.stable_pair.pre_read
  + require seed.kind is regular_file
  + [relative_path] is Some exact plan.relative_path
  + [kind] is exact seed.kind
  + [mode_class] is exact validated plan.mode_class
  + [attributes] is exact seed.attributes
  + [identity] is exact seed.identity
  + [number_of_links] is exact seed.number_of_links
  + [streams] is exact seed.streams in its current canonical seed order
  + [length] is exact seed.length
  + [content_sha256] is Some exact binding.content_observation.derived_sha256
  + [observation_ordinal] is exact plan.observation_ordinal
  - never: default, normalize, recompute, discard, reorder, synthesize, or substitute a mapped field

& [M2AValidationContract] reuses current authority
  + invoke ValidateTopologyForm::validate on the completed TopologyEntryObservation
  + current M2A validation owns descendant-path grammar, strong identity, link, stream, kind, mode, length, digest, and ordinal structural coherence
  + an M2A rejection returns topology_form with the exact nested TopologyFormFault
  + nested topology fault is boxed to keep the outer Result error bounded in size
  - never: replace current validation with a weaker local approximation
  - never: interpret validation success as observation, admission, or physical truth

& [ComponentJoinContract] is exact
  + evaluate only after M2A validation succeeds
  + take the final slash-separated relative-path component without normalization
  + require exact String equality with binding.stable_pair.pre_read.policy_decision.component
  + prerequisite stability proves the pre-read and post-read policy decisions are exactly equal
  + mismatch returns component fault
  - never: case fold, Unicode normalize, trim, resolve, canonicalize, join to a root, inspect a filesystem, or claim physical path binding

& [ModeMeaningContract] is declaration only
  + accepted mode is copied from the caller plan
  + Windows attributes remain an independent mapped seed fact
  + this slice performs no Git lookup, tree comparison, index query, extension inference, or platform-mode inference
  - never: describe accepted mode as Git-observed, reconciled, or authoritative

& [OrdinalMeaningContract] is declaration only
  + accepted ordinal is copied from the caller plan after a nonzero gate
  + no single-entry rule proves monotonicity, uniqueness, contiguity, canonical order, or traversal ownership
  - never: describe accepted ordinal as scanner-assigned or inventory-valid

& [OutputContract] preserves complete lineage
  + [profile] is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-regular-file-topology-projection/0.1
  + [plan] preserves the complete validated placement plan
  + [content_binding] preserves the complete consumed supplied-content stable binding
  + [topology_observation] preserves the complete validated M2A projection
  + [inspection] is immutable getters plus serde Serialize
  + [construction] is private to successful projection
  - never: derive Deserialize, implement Default, expose public fields or mutable getters, or provide a public constructor
  - never: implement From or Into conversion that returns a bare TopologyEntryObservation and loses the wrapper

& [FaultContract] is closed and bounded
  + [codes] are json, profile, projection_identity, entry_reference_identity, entry_reference, component, mode, ordinal, kind, topology_form, and resource
  + [nested_topology_fault] is present exactly for topology_form and absent otherwise
  + [field] is deterministic and no longer than 64 Unicode scalar values
  + [message] is deterministic and no longer than 256 Unicode scalar values
  + [release] is exactly one fault with no plan, binding, topology form, partial wrapper, or resumable success value
  - never: disclose content chunks, hash state, complete encoded input, or serialized binding

& [EvaluationOrderContract] is exact
  + [step_1] pre-decode encoded-plan cap when decoding
  + [step_2] strict JSON decode
  + [step_3] exact profile
  + [step_4] projection identity
  + [step_5] entry-reference identity
  + [step_6] regular mode
  + [step_7] observation ordinal
  + [step_8] plan-to-binding entry-reference equality
  + [step_9] exact candidate mapping
  + [step_10] current M2A validation
  + [step_11] exact final-component equality
  + [step_12] output-only wrapper
  = must: release the first deterministic failure in this order

& [SemanticStrengthContract] prevents provenance inflation
  + [derived] metadata and digest fields are exact transforms of previously accepted supplied values
  + [declared] placement fields are exact caller plan values
  + [correlated] entry reference and final component pass exact equality gates
  + [projected] complete M2A form passes structural validation and remains nested with its lineage
  + [physical] is absent
  + [admitted] is absent
  - never: claim physical origin, existence, root membership, same-object or same-epoch provenance, stream completeness, actual time order, Git truth, traversal truth, trust, authenticity, freshness, atomic snapshot, immutability, admission, receipt, or mutation safety

& [DataDesignContract] is explicit
  + [conceptual_model] join derived supplied evidence and declared placement under exact structural relations
  + [logical_model] strict plan plus output-only binding to gates to candidate to current validation to wrapper
  + [physical_model] safe deterministic in-memory Rust using serde and existing crate modules
  + [source_data] placement plan and supplied-content stable binding
  + [derived_projection] complete M2A topology observation inside lineage wrapper
  + [identity_namespace] caller-owned and invocation local
  + [state] absent
  + [persistence] absent

& [ImplementationBoundary] is zero effect
  + [authorized_file] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/windows_supplied_regular_file_topology_projection.rs
  + [authorized_export] is one exact library-module export
  + [authorized_tests] are module unit tests, one independent static test, one evidence rehash test, and workspace regression tests
  + [plan_json_byte_cap] is 262144
  + [message_scalar_cap] is 256
  + [field_scalar_cap] is 64
  + [Cargo_delta] is zero
  + [lockfile_delta] is zero
  + [unsafe] is denied
  + [production_imports] are std formatting, serde, topology_forms, windows_supplied_entry_observation seed support, and windows_supplied_content_digest binding support
  - never: use windows-sys, filesystem, path resolution, process, environment, clock, random, network, persistence, database, model, handle, pointer, buffer, platform query, Git, traversal, inventory, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, cleanup, review execution, or promotion APIs

& [RequirementSet] is M2B-SRTP-001 through M2B-SRTP-014
  + [requirements] are strict plan, local identities, binding-only input, exact reference join, current M2A validation, exact component join, regular mode, nonzero ordinal, exact mapping, nested topology fault, output-only wrapper, bounded atomic faults, semantic nonclaims, and proof closure

& [AcceptanceContract] is exact
  + [source] manifest matches exact SHA-256 and byte count
  + [authority] governing signature binds every SJS stage and both current prerequisite signatures
  + [focused] module unit tests and one independent static test pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [behavior] every requirement, evaluation stage, mapping edge, fault, bound, and output rule has a direct test or static proof edge
  + [effects] Cargo, lockfile, dependency, unsafe, platform, and runtime-effect deltas remain zero
  + [evidence] clone-portable manifest hashes canonical, module, tests, solution, proof, review, and narratives
  + [global] workspace debug and overflow-checked release tests, format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, audit, and recursive evidence closure pass
  + [downstream_gate] directory projection, inventory reconciliation, physical producer, Git reconciliation, traversal, receipt, and admission remain absent

& [AuthorityBoundary] is pure implementation only
  + [allowed] one deterministic module, export, serialization, focused tests, static test, evidence support, solution, proof, review, and governed narrative
  + [forbidden] every physical, platform, filesystem, Git, traversal, receipt, admission, and mutation-related behavior or claim

